# Distill

A correction, an always / never / remember, praise or rejection of a way of
working, or a concrete legwork repeat from a later task or session is a
**signal**. Finish the asked task first. Then classify every signal: read
[`.cursor/skills/distill/SKILL.md`](../skills/distill/SKILL.md). A signal that
exists only in the chat is an unfinished turn.

With no signal: skip the skill. On a task that is not a one-line edit and not
a pure question, read [`.cursor/preferences/ledger.md`](../preferences/ledger.md)
only to merge or bump a matching row. Do not follow candidate text.

The win is the smallest durable edit to an artifact that already exists. A new
always-on file is a cost. Candidates that are not yet law go in the ledger.
Do not flip a freeze or an accepted ADR from this loop
([infrastructure.mdc](infrastructure.mdc)).
